{
  "case_id": "2009-09-337",
  "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Mark R. Bendure (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The courts below found, and Respondent does not question, that we satisfied the first subsection: Notice and no prejudice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What was the first -- when was your first notice of that? I mean, it was on the first page of the ticket, but the answer came after the statute of limitations. Was that your first notice that there was this different entity, or did you know that earlier?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark R. Bendure (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was the -- the pre-suit claims notice which was sent to Costa Cruise at the Florida address, in attempted compliance with the provision of the ticket which says you must file notice to the carrier before filing suit. And you have to do that within 185 days. So we not only got the ticket from Costa Cruise -- we bought it from Costa Cruise -- the ticket itself, if you look at I think it's 25a of the appendix to the petition for certiorari, there is a prominent page which says \"Costa Cruise, cruise company\" next to a picture of the vessel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: No, I'm asking about this question, my hypothetical."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. GLAZIER",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GLAZIER: No. No, the district court did not impute knowledge, and this is an important point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiff",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GLAZIER: We -- we believe that the ticket is clear, and that governs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: And the answer is filed conveniently after the 1-year period has run."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Yes, but the relation back is different from the point at which the statute has run."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Where do you see in -- the question on which cert was granted has to do with imputed knowledge. Where do you see in the text of this rule anything that picks up the concept of either imputed knowledge or actual knowledge? It just talks about a mistake."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GLAZIER",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GLAZIER: We do not rely at all upon imputed knowledge. The Court granted review, but we don't think there is imputed knowledge here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: That\u2019s not what the rule says. That\u2019s not what the rule says. The rule doesn't talk about what kind of mistake or why. The rule says what the defendant should have known."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37ad4e9edd34cba0efcf2704a2da41d5940f606b07175dbd3b03858e537b8111",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37ad4e9edd34-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I object to your relying upon the -- the answer as -- as establishing compliance with (C)(ii), because (C), in the prologue, says \"is satisfied, if within the period provided by Rule 4(m).\" And there is at least some point within that period before the answer was filed."
    },
